🔧 Jenkins Pipeline Integration Documentation

This documentation explains how the Jenkins pipeline is structured for the automation project, what each file is responsible for, and how the execution flows from application startup to suite execution, result collection, artifact handling, and application shutdown.

The objective is to make the Jenkins integration easier to understand, maintain, troubleshoot, and evolve.

✅ With this documentation, any maintainer should be able to:
Understand the end to end Jenkins execution flow
Identify which file is responsible for each part of the process
Know where to change suite configuration and execution order
Know where startup and shutdown logic is handled
Understand how suite logs, screenshots, and metadata are collected
Troubleshoot failures more quickly when the pipeline stops before, during, or after execution
